# Re-grounded from UC-SST-004 (Create Scale Site) onto the new React app: route /scale-sites/create,
# components/Form/ScaleSiteForm -> POST /api/scale-sites (ScaleSiteService.createScaleSite). Success is
# PROVEN by an API read-back of GET /api/scale-sites/{id}/summary (full record incl. site types), not the
# redirect alone.
#
# DATA GAP (test-env, NOT an app bug): the scale-site PK is generated by a BEFORE-INSERT trigger
# (THE.SCS_SCST_BR_IU_TRG) that reads THE.INTEGER_NUMBER, which the one-hop real-data extract left EMPTY —
# so create 500s until it is seeded. Unblocked by scs-real-test-data-patches/sst/integer-number-seed.sql
# (apply-patches.sh). Verified live 2026-08-12 -> HTTP 201. Owner 00105328/00, org unit 27, method codes
# W/P are pinned in fixtures/sst/scale-site-test-data.ts. There is NO delete endpoint, so each created
# site is removed at the DB on teardown and proven gone via GET -> 404.
#
# @mode:serial — the create happy path (S01) is the suite's ONLY scale-site create. The legacy min-free-id
# PK trigger (SCS_SCST_BR_IU_TRG) races under concurrent creates (ORA-00001 -> HTTP 500; see
# defects.md "concurrency" note), so we do not run the two scenarios in this file in parallel with each
# other; the page object also bounded-retries a transient collision. A normal single-pass run issues one
# create, so this is belt-and-suspenders for the --repeat-each stress gate.
@sst @UC-SST-004 @mode:serial
Feature: Create Scale Site

  @S01 @p0
  Scenario: Create a scale site with the required fields and site types
    Given I am on the Scale Site create form
    When I create a scale site with valid details
    Then the scale site is created
    And the created scale site reads back with its name, owner, and site types

  # Entry-point variation (S07): the "Create Scale Site" button on the scale-site search results (rendered
  # after a search) routes to the same create form.
  @S07 @p2
  Scenario: Reach the create form from the scale site search results
    Given I have run a scale site search
    When I click Create Scale Site in the results
    Then the Scale Site create form is shown
